---
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
// TODO: legal review by the firm. This is a POPIA notice template, not a final notice.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Makhafola & Associates Inc. collects, uses and protects personal information under the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA)."
  namespace="privacy"
>
  <Container class="pt-36 pb-12 md:pt-44 md:pb-16">
    <h1 data-reveal-heading class="font-heading text-h1 font-semibold">
      Privacy notice
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-ink-muted">
      This notice explains how {site.name} handles personal information under the Protection of Personal
      Information Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA).
    </p>
  </Container>

  <Container class="grid grid-cols-1 border-t border-rule pt-12 pb-24 md:pt-16 md:pb-32 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
    <div class="prose lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-2">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you contact us through this website, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, email address and, if you give it, your phone number;</li>
        <li>the practice area you choose and the message you write;</li>
        <li>
          technical information needed to protect the form from abuse (a Cloudflare Turnstile check, which
          processes your IP address and browser signals).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you become a client, we also collect the identity documents and information that the Financial
        Intelligence Centre Act (FICA) requires, and the information needed to act on your matter.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to respond to your enquiry;</li>
        <li>to assess whether we can act for you, including conflict checks;</li>
        <li>to provide legal services and keep the records our profession requires;</li>
        <li>to meet our legal obligations, including under FICA.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for marketing without your consent.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share personal information only where needed: with service providers who host this website and
        deliver email on our behalf (under agreements that require them to protect it), with courts, counsel
        and other parties as your matter requires, and with authorities where the law requires it. Some
        providers may process information outside South Africa, and we only use providers subject to adequate
        data protection.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not lead to an engagement are deleted when they are no longer needed to respond to
        you. Client records are kept for the periods required by law and by the rules of the Legal Practice
        Council, after which they are destroyed or de-identified.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under POPIA you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask whether we hold personal information about you, and request access to it;</li>
        <li>
          ask us to correct or delete personal information that is inaccurate, out of date or unlawfully held;
        </li>
        <li>object to the processing of your personal information on reasonable grounds;</li>
        <li>lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>This website does not set advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

      <h2>Contacting the Information Officer</h2>
      <p>
        Address requests or questions about this notice to our Information Officer at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or {site.address.lines.join(", ")}.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may also contact the Information Regulator (South Africa) through its website,{" "}
        <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
          inforegulator.org.za
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
